        "params": {
          "text": "SMALL-ANGLE DOUBLE PENDULUM (m1=m2=l1=l2=1, g=9.81)\nLinearized equations: \u03b81\u2033 = -2g\u00b7\u03b81 + g\u00b7\u03b82; \u03b82\u2033 = 2g\u00b7\u03b81 - 2g\u00b7\u03b82.\nEuler step: 1 ms. Initial angles: \u03b81=0.2 rad, \u03b82=0.1 rad. Scope plots both angles.\nThis is the small-angle linear model; the full nonlinear equations require signal division.",
